<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="50–60 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 3</p>
  <h1>Future intentions with <em>be going to</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Connect a future idea to something that exists now: <span class="ex">The team decided yesterday. They’re going to run a repair workshop.</span> <span class="ex">That loose sign is going to fall.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">prior intention · present evidence</span>
    <span class="tag">am / is / are going to</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Compare an earlier decision with present evidence.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Connect meaning to be + going to + base verb.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Control form and separate intentions from nearby future choices.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Present a fictional community-workshop plan.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can report a prior intention, predict a result from present evidence, form statements and questions, and explain why a nearby future form fits a different context.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved the present-continuous frame, a completed past decision, and present be agreement.">
    <h3>Three checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the stated time and the complete verb system.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier lesson choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is meeting">is meeting</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="meets">meets</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="decided">decided</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="decides">decides</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The calendar shows a fixed appointment tomorrow at 9:00: The technician <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is meeting" data-hint="A scheduled personal arrangement can use the present continuous." data-fix="The technician is meeting the manager tomorrow at 9:00." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the manager tomorrow at 9:00.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The planning notes record one completed decision yesterday: The team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="decided" data-hint="Yesterday places the completed decision in the past." data-fix="The team decided on the workshop plan yesterday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the workshop plan yesterday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The live photo shows several boxes in the room now: The boxes <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="The plural subject boxes takes are." data-fix="The boxes are beside the door now." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> beside the door now.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice what exists before the future event</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor Center workshop</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Yesterday, Rina and Lee decided to offer a free repair workshop. They’re going to invite twelve neighbors. They aren’t going to charge a fee.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Now Lee points to a tall stack of boxes. “That top box is going to fall.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which future actions come from intentions that existed before this conversation?</li>
      <li>Which sentence is not anyone’s intention? What present evidence supports it?</li>
      <li>Find the form of <span class="ex">be</span>, <span class="ex">going to</span>, and the base verb in each sentence.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You connected each form to a prior intention, present evidence, polarity, or question purpose.">
    <h3>Discovery check: connect form and meaning</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="prior intention">prior intention</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="present evidence">present evidence</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="invite">invite</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="aren’t">aren’t</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Are">Are</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The team made the decision yesterday, so <span class="ex">They’re going to invite twelve neighbors</span> reports a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="prior intention" data-hint="The decision already existed before the current conversation." data-fix="The invitation plan is a prior intention." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The top box is leaning now, so <span class="ex">It’s going to fall</span> is a prediction from <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="present evidence" data-hint="The box’s current position supports the prediction." data-fix="The prediction comes from present evidence." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The plural subject team members needs the form: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="They agrees with are before going to." data-fix="They are going to invite twelve neighbors." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to invite twelve neighbors.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>After <span class="ex">going to</span>, use the base verb: They’re going to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="invite" data-hint="Going to is followed by the base verb, not invited or inviting." data-fix="They’re going to invite twelve neighbors." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> twelve neighbors.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The decision excludes a fee: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="aren’t" data-hint="Not attaches to the be verb in a negative." data-fix="They aren’t going to charge a fee." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to charge a fee.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>To ask the group about its intention, move be first: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Are" data-hint="A question with they begins Are they going to." data-fix="Are they going to invite twelve neighbors?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> they going to invite twelve neighbors?</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: a present basis for a future idea</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Be going to</span> presents a future event from a basis that exists now. That basis can be a person’s prior intention or present evidence that points toward a result. The form does not make the future certain.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>present basis</th><th>example</th><th>speaker’s message</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>prior intention</td><td><span class="ex">We’re going to run a repair workshop.</span></td><td>we decided before speaking</td></tr>
      <tr><td>present evidence</td><td><span class="ex">That loose sign is going to fall.</span></td><td>what I can see now supports the prediction</td></tr>
      <tr><td>no stated basis</td><td><span class="ex">Maybe the workshop will become popular.</span></td><td>a neutral prediction, not a visible result</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">A future-time expression does not choose the form. <span class="ex">Tomorrow</span> can appear with <span class="ex">going to</span>, the present continuous, <span class="ex">will</span>, or another future expression. The context and the speaker’s meaning choose the form.</p>

  <h2>Build the form: be + going to + base verb</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>purpose</th><th>I</th><th>he / she / it</th><th>you / we / they</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>positive</td><td><span class="ex">I’m going to call.</span></td><td><span class="ex">She’s going to call.</span></td><td><span class="ex">They’re going to call.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>negative</td><td><span class="ex">I’m not going to call.</span></td><td><span class="ex">She isn’t going to call.</span></td><td><span class="ex">They aren’t going to call.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>question</td><td><span class="ex">Am I going to call?</span></td><td><span class="ex">Is she going to call?</span></td><td><span class="ex">Are they going to call?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>short answer</td><td><span class="ex">Yes, I am.</span></td><td><span class="ex">No, she isn’t.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Yes, they are.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Am</span>, <span class="ex">is</span>, or <span class="ex">are</span> carries agreement, moves before the subject in a question, and combines with <span class="ex">not</span>. Do not add <span class="ex">do</span> or <span class="ex">does</span>. The next verb stays in its base form.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled agreement, negatives, questions, short answers, and the base verb after going to.">
    <h3>Drill 1: complete the workshop plan</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Going-to form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="isn’t">isn’t</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="aren’t">aren’t</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Is">Is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Are">Are</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="bring">bring</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Rina reports her intention: I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="am" data-hint="The subject I takes am." data-fix="I am going to call the volunteers." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to call the volunteers.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Lee’s prior plan uses singular agreement: He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="The singular subject he takes is." data-fix="He is going to check the tools." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to check the tools.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Several volunteers share an intention: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="The plural subject they takes are." data-fix="They are going to move the tables." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to move the tables.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The plan excludes a fee: Rina <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="isn’t" data-hint="A singular negative uses isn’t going to." data-fix="Rina isn’t going to charge a fee." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to charge a fee.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The plan excludes food sales: The volunteers <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="aren’t" data-hint="The plural negative volunteers takes aren’t." data-fix="The volunteers aren’t going to sell food." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to sell food.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Ask yes or no about Lee’s prior intention: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Is" data-hint="A question about Lee begins Is Lee going to." data-fix="Is Lee going to check the tools?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> Lee going to check the tools?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Ask about several volunteers: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Are" data-hint="A question about the plural volunteers begins Are." data-fix="Are the volunteers going to move the tables?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the volunteers going to move the tables?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The approved plan lists the base verb: They’re going to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="bring" data-hint="After going to, use the base verb bring." data-fix="They’re going to bring extra chairs." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> extra chairs.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose meaning, not just a future time</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>context</th><th>natural choice</th><th>why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>decision made yesterday</td><td><span class="ex">We’re going to invite neighbors.</span></td><td>prior intention</td></tr>
      <tr><td>appointment fixed for 9:00</td><td><span class="ex">The technician is coming at 9:00.</span></td><td>organized arrangement with a concrete detail</td></tr>
      <tr><td>phone rings; decision made now</td><td><span class="ex">I’ll answer it.</span></td><td>decision at the moment of speaking</td></tr>
      <tr><td>box is leaning</td><td><span class="ex">It’s going to fall.</span></td><td>prediction from present evidence</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>An intention and an arrangement can both be true. The speaker chooses a viewpoint. <span class="ex">We’re going to meet the technician</span> highlights the plan; <span class="ex">We’re meeting the technician at 9:00</span> presents the organized appointment. A time expression alone does not prove either meaning.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3><span class="ex">Going to go</span> is grammatical</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">We’re going to go to the center after lunch</span> reports an intention and is correct. <span class="ex">We’re going to the center after lunch</span> uses present continuous for a planned movement or arrangement. Speakers often prefer the shorter sentence when the context is clear, but the repeated words are not an error.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You used context to separate a prior intention, an arrangement, a now-decision, an evidence prediction, movement, and a time phrase.">
    <h3>Drill 2: choose the future viewpoint</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Future meaning choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are going to invite">are going to invite</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is coming">is coming</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I’ll answer">I’ll answer</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is going to fall">is going to fall</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are going to go">are going to go</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="next Saturday">next Saturday</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The notes say the group decided yesterday: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are going to invite" data-hint="The decision existed before this conversation, so going to presents a prior intention." data-fix="They are going to invite twelve neighbors." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> twelve neighbors.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The calendar confirms the appointment at exactly 9:00 Saturday: The technician <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is coming" data-hint="A fixed appointment with a concrete time is presented as an arrangement." data-fix="The technician is coming at 9:00 Saturday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at 9:00 Saturday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The phone rings unexpectedly, and Rina decides at that moment: “<button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="I’ll answer" data-hint="The decision happens now, at the moment Rina speaks." data-fix="The phone is ringing. I’ll answer it." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> it.”</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The top box is leaning farther over the edge right now: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is going to fall" data-hint="The present position of the box is visible evidence for the prediction." data-fix="The top box is going to fall." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The group decided yesterday to travel together after lunch: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are going to go" data-hint="Going to go is grammatical when going to marks a prior intention and go names the movement." data-fix="They are going to go to the center after lunch." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to the center after lunch.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>No preposition comes before this time phrase: The workshop is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="next Saturday" data-hint="Use next Saturday without on." data-fix="The workshop is next Saturday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: contractions, stress, and <em>gonna</em></h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In relaxed U.S. English, speakers usually contract <span class="ex">be</span>: <span class="ex">I’m</span>, <span class="ex">she’s</span>, <span class="ex">we’re</span>. They reduce <span class="ex">going to</span> and stress the important verb or result: <span class="ex">We’re gonna <strong>CALL</strong> the volunteers. That box is gonna <strong>FALL</strong>.</span></p>
  <p><span class="ex">Gonna</span> is a useful listening form before a verb, but standard writing uses <span class="ex">going to</span>. It cannot replace movement followed only by a place. Say <span class="ex">I’m going to the center</span>, not <span class="ex">I’m gonna the center</span>. In a yes-or-no question, let the voice rise and keep the form of <span class="ex">be</span> clear: <span class="ex"><strong>ARE</strong>-you-gonna <strong>CALL</strong>?</span></p>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read intention, arrangement, now-decision, evidence, negative, and movement listening check">
    <h2>Listen: what is the speaker’s basis?</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Your teacher reads each fictional line once naturally and once more slowly. Listen for the speaker’s basis and the reduced spoken form. Open the script only after checking.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard a prior intention, an arrangement, a decision made now, present evidence, a negative plan, and movement to a place.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening check</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a plan decided yesterday" data-hint="The speaker says they agreed on the plan yesterday." data-fix="They agreed yesterday, so the invitation is a prior intention."><p class="quiz-question">1. What is the basis for Clip 1?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a plan decided yesterday">a plan decided yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a decision made while speaking">a decision made while speaking</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a regular habit">a regular habit</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a fixed appointment" data-hint="The calendar and exact 9:00 time present an organized arrangement." data-fix="The technician is coming at 9:00 for a fixed appointment."><p class="quiz-question">2. What does Clip 2 present?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a fixed appointment">a fixed appointment</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a visible prediction">a visible prediction</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a past event">a past event</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Rina decides to answer now" data-hint="The unexpected ring creates the decision at the moment of speaking." data-fix="The phone rings, and Rina decides now: I’ll answer it."><p class="quiz-question">3. What happens in Clip 3?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rina decides to answer now">Rina decides to answer now</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rina reports an old plan">Rina reports an old plan</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rina refuses to answer">Rina refuses to answer</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the box is leaning" data-hint="The visible position of the box supports the result." data-fix="The box is leaning, so it is going to fall."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which evidence supports Clip 4?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the box is leaning">the box is leaning</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the box fell yesterday">the box fell yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="someone wants the box to fall">someone wants the box to fall</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="they do not intend to charge" data-hint="Listen for aren’t before going to." data-fix="They aren’t going to charge, so the fee is excluded from their plan."><p class="quiz-question">5. What does Clip 5 mean?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="they do not intend to charge">they do not intend to charge</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="they already charged">they already charged</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="they may increase the fee">they may increase the fee</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="movement to the center" data-hint="Going is followed directly by the place phrase to the center, not by another verb." data-fix="We’re going to the center describes movement to a place."><p class="quiz-question">6. What does <span class="ex">going</span> express in Clip 6?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="movement to the center">movement to the center</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a prediction from evidence">a prediction from evidence</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a negative intention">a negative intention</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details class="thinking-card">
      <summary>Open the teacher script after checking</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">We agreed yesterday. We’re going to invite twelve neighbors.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The calendar is confirmed. The technician is coming at nine.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The phone is ringing. I’ll answer it.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">Look at that leaning box. It’s going to fall.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">They aren’t going to charge a fee.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">We’re going to the center after lunch.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Read the planning update</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Message to the Harbor Center team</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">We agreed yesterday to run the repair workshop next Saturday. Rina is going to call twelve neighbors, and Lee is going to check the tools. We aren’t going to charge a fee. The technician is coming at 9:00, so that appointment is already on the calendar. One warning: the outdoor sign is loose and moving in the wind. It’s going to fall if we do not secure it. I just heard the delivery bell, so I’ll open the door.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You located the prior intention, the fixed arrangement, and the present evidence in the update.">
    <h3>Read, then choose the exact evidence</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the team agreed yesterday" data-hint="The opening sentence states when the workshop decision was made." data-fix="The team agreed yesterday, before this message."><p class="quiz-question">1. What proves that the workshop is a prior intention?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the team agreed yesterday">the team agreed yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the bell just rang">the bell just rang</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the sign is loose">the sign is loose</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the technician is coming at 9:00" data-hint="The update identifies one calendar appointment with an exact time." data-fix="The technician is coming at 9:00 is the fixed arrangement."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence presents the fixed arrangement?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the technician is coming at 9:00">the technician is coming at 9:00</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rina is going to call neighbors">Rina is going to call neighbors</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’ll open the door">I’ll open the door</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the sign is loose and moving" data-hint="The sign’s current condition supports the prediction." data-fix="The sign is loose and moving, so the writer predicts it is going to fall."><p class="quiz-question">3. What present evidence supports the prediction?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the sign is loose and moving">the sign is loose and moving</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the workshop is free">the workshop is free</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the calendar is confirmed">the calendar is confirmed</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the intention and the question</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="rina is going to call twelve neighbors" data-hint="Begin with Rina, add is going to, then the base verb and its object." data-fix="Rina is going to call twelve neighbors." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence reports Rina’s prior intention with is going to plus the base verb call.">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the intention</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The plan was decided yesterday.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="neighbors">neighbors</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="rina">Rina</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="call">call</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="going">going</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="twelve">twelve</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="are they going to charge a fee" data-hint="Move Are before they, then keep going to plus the base verb charge." data-fix="Are they going to charge a fee?" data-success-message="Correct. The question moves Are before the subject and keeps charge in the base form.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Ask yes or no about the team’s fee plan.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="fee">fee</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">Are</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="charge">charge</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="going">going</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="they">they</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair three high-value errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="invite" data-hint="After going to, the activity verb must stay in its base form." data-fix="They are going to invite twelve neighbors." data-why="Going to is followed by the base verb, so inviting must become invite." data-success-message="Correct. You restored the base verb after going to.">
    <h3>Drill 5: use the base verb</h3><p>The plan says, “They are going to inviting twelve neighbors.” Tap the word to repair.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="they">They</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="going">going to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="invite">inviting</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="neighbors">twelve neighbors.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="does" data-hint="A going-to question moves Is before Lee and does not use does." data-fix="Is Lee going to check the tools?" data-why="Is already carries agreement and builds the question, so does would mix two question systems." data-success-message="Correct. You removed do-support and restored the going-to question system.">
    <h3>Drill 6: keep one question system</h3><p>The coordinator asks, “Does Lee is going to check the tools?” Tap the word to remove.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="does">Does</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="lee">Lee</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="going">going to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="check">check the tools?</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="gonna-place" data-hint="Gonna can reduce going to before a verb, but it cannot be followed directly by a place." data-fix="I’m going to the center after lunch." data-why="Going expresses movement here and is followed by the place phrase to the center. There is no following base verb for gonna." data-success-message="Correct. You kept full going when it is the movement verb before a place.">
    <h3>Drill 7: movement or reduced future form?</h3><p>The message says, “I’m gonna the center after lunch.” Tap the opening to repair.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="gonna-place">I’m gonna</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="center">the center</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="after">after lunch.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transform: keep the intended future viewpoint</h3>
    <p>Say every response before revealing it.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I decided yesterday to call the volunteers. Report the prior intention.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I’m going to call the volunteers.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Rina is going to charge a fee. Make the plan negative.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Rina isn’t going to charge a fee.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> They’re going to move the tables. Ask yes or no.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Are they going to move the tables?</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> The sign is loose and moving. Predict the result with fall.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The sign is going to fall.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> The calendar confirms Saturday at 9:00. Present the technician’s visit as an arrangement.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The technician is coming at 9:00 Saturday.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> The phone rings unexpectedly. Decide now to answer it.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I’ll answer it.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it: present a fictional community plan</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real work, study, home, location, schedule, travel, family, relationships, finances, devices, health, or future plans. Use the fictional workshop, invent a public event, or share personal information only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Establish the prior decisions:</b> Choose a fictional event and say when the organizers decided. Report three intentions with <span class="ex">going to</span>, including one negative.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Add one arrangement:</b> Put one appointment on a fictional calendar with a concrete time or place. Present it with the present continuous and explain the difference in viewpoint.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Respond to new evidence:</b> Describe one safe, fictional situation visible now and make a <span class="ex">going to</span> prediction. Then create one unexpected event and make a decision with <span class="ex">will</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: give a 45–60 second planning update.</b> Include three prior intentions, one negative, one going-to question, one fixed arrangement, one evidence-based prediction, and one decision made now. End by asking the listener which future choice had a prior basis.</div>

  <h2>Final check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You controlled prior intention, present evidence, form, arrangement, now-decision, movement, and spoken reduction.">
    <h3>Eight decisions from a new library event</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="are going to organize" data-hint="The organizers decided last Monday, before this conversation." data-fix="They are going to organize a book exchange."><p class="quiz-question">1. The organizers decided last Monday: They ___ a book exchange.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are going to organize">are going to organize</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="organize now">organize now</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="were organizing">were organizing</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="isn’t going to sell" data-hint="One organizer’s negative intention uses isn’t going to plus the base verb sell." data-fix="Maya isn’t going to sell any books."><p class="quiz-question">2. Maya’s plan excludes sales: She ___ any books.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="isn’t going to sell">isn’t going to sell</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="doesn’t going to sell">doesn’t going to sell</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="isn’t going to selling">isn’t going to selling</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Are the volunteers going to bring tables?" data-hint="A plural going-to question moves Are before the volunteers." data-fix="Are the volunteers going to bring tables?"><p class="quiz-question">3. Which question asks about the volunteers’ prior plan?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Are the volunteers going to bring tables?">Are the volunteers going to bring tables?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do the volunteers going to bring tables?">Do the volunteers going to bring tables?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Is the volunteers going to bring tables?">Is the volunteers going to bring tables?</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is going to spill" data-hint="The cup is visibly tipping now, so present evidence supports the prediction." data-fix="The cup is going to spill."><p class="quiz-question">4. A full cup is tipping over the table’s edge right now: It ___.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is going to spill">is going to spill</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="spills every day">spills every day</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="was going to spill">was going to spill</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is meeting" data-hint="The calendar confirms an organized appointment at an exact time." data-fix="Maya is meeting the librarian at 8:30 Saturday."><p class="quiz-question">5. The calendar confirms Maya’s appointment with the librarian at 8:30 Saturday: She ___ the librarian then.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is meeting">is meeting</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="meets yesterday">meets yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="was meeting">was meeting</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I’ll get it" data-hint="The knock is unexpected, and the speaker decides at that moment." data-fix="Someone is knocking. I’ll get it."><p class="quiz-question">6. Someone knocks unexpectedly, and you decide at that moment to open the door: “___.”</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’ll get it">I’ll get it</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I got it yesterday">I got it yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’m getting it every day">I’m getting it every day</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="We’re going to go to the library" data-hint="Going to go can report a prior intention to move to a place." data-fix="We’re going to go to the library after lunch."><p class="quiz-question">7. Which sentence is grammatical for a travel intention decided yesterday?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We’re going to go to the library">We’re going to go to the library</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We’re going to going to the library">We’re going to going to the library</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We going to go to the library">We going to go to the library</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I’m going to the library" data-hint="Going is the movement verb before the place phrase to the library, so gonna cannot replace it." data-fix="In standard writing and natural movement language, write I’m going to the library."><p class="quiz-question">8. Which sentence correctly describes movement to a place and also fits standard writing?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’m going to the library">I’m going to the library</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’m gonna the library">I’m gonna the library</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I gonna to the library">I gonna to the library</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect and plan the next use</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Can you explain the choice?</h3>
    <p>Explain the present basis in <span class="ex">We’re going to run a workshop</span> and <span class="ex">That sign is going to fall</span>. Then explain why <span class="ex">The technician is coming at 9:00</span> and <span class="ex">I’ll answer the phone</span> use different future viewpoints.</p>
    <p>Choose your next use: repeat the planning update with fewer notes, ask four intention questions, or complete the retrieval below tomorrow.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="note-line">Return tomorrow before rereading. Complete the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute next-day retrieval</a>, then revisit only the meaning, form, boundary, or spoken pattern that still feels slow.</p>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day prior-intention and present-evidence retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a prior intention, a fixed arrangement, and an evidence-based prediction.">
      <h3>Choose from memory before looking back</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Next-day future choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are going to invite">are going to invite</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="invited">invited</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is coming">is coming</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="comes every day">comes every day</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is going to fall">is going to fall</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fell yesterday">fell yesterday</button></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The notes say the organizers decided yesterday: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are going to invite" data-hint="A decision that existed before today is a prior intention." data-fix="They are going to invite twelve neighbors." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> twelve neighbors.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The appointment is confirmed for exactly 9:00 Saturday: The technician <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is coming" data-hint="The exact confirmed appointment is presented as an arrangement." data-fix="The technician is coming at 9:00 Saturday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at 9:00.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The loose sign is moving farther away from the wall right now: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is going to fall" data-hint="The sign’s current movement provides present evidence." data-fix="The sign is going to fall." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="does" data-hint="A going-to question begins Are and needs no do-support." data-fix="Are they going to charge a fee?" data-why="Are carries agreement and builds the question, so does would mix two question systems." data-success-message="Correct. You restored the going-to question system.">
      <h3>Repair one high-risk question</h3><p>The visitor asks, “Does they are going to charge a fee?” Tap the word to remove.</p>
      <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="does">Does</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="they">they</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="going">going to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="charge">charge a fee?</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Thirty-second retrieval</h3>
      <p>Without looking back, give one prior intention, one negative, one going-to question, one evidence-based prediction, one fixed arrangement, and one decision made now.</p>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
      <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We’re going to run a workshop. We aren’t going to charge. Are you going to invite neighbors? That sign is going to fall. The technician is coming at nine. I’ll answer the phone.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>
